IMPORT daydate

-- Social Security Act 1991 (Cth), Chapter 5 -- the date arithmetic the debt questions need, kept in one small module so that
-- the daydate library is imported once (see NOTES.md). Every other module of this encoding imports this one.

§ `Dates for the debt provisions`

-- A day is counted as its day number, so "the 28th day after the date of the notice" is the notice's day number plus 28.
@desc The day number of a date (days since the start of the calendar), for counting periods of days
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day number of` `the day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the day`

@desc The date a given number of days after a date
GIVEN `days` IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` `days` `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS `days`)

@desc The number of days in the calendar year a date falls in: 366 in a leap year, otherwise 365
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in the calendar year of` `the day` MEANS `Days in year` (DATE_YEAR `the day`)

@desc The month (1 to 12) of a date
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the month of` `the day` MEANS DATE_MONTH `the day`

@desc The year of a date
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year of` `the day` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the day`

@desc Whether the first date is on or before the second
GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first` `is on or before` `the second` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the second`
